#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:15
msgid "What has been changed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:17
msgid ""
"The CI4 model has much more functionality, including automatic database "
"connection, basic CRUD, in-model validation, and automatic pagination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:18
msgid ""
"Since namespaces has been added to CodeIgniter 4, the models must be "
"changed to support namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:21
msgid "Upgrade Guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:23
msgid "First, move all model files to the folder **app/Models**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:24
msgid "Add this line just after the opening php tag: ``namespace App\\Models;``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:25
msgid ""
"Below the ``namespace App\\Models;`` line add this line: ``use "
"CodeIgniter\\Model;``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:26
msgid "Replace ``extends CI_Model`` with ``extends Model``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:27
msgid "Add the ``protected $table`` property and set the table name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:28
msgid ""
"Add the ``protected $allowedFields`` property and set the array of field "
"names to allow to insert/update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:29
msgid ""
"Instead of CI3's ``$this->load->model('x');``, you would now use "
"``$this->x = new X();``, following namespaced conventions for your "
"component. Alternatively, you can use the :php:func:`model()` function: "
"``$this->x = model('X');``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:31
msgid ""
"If you use sub-directories in your model structure you have to change the"
" namespace according to that. Example: You have a version 3 model located"
" in **application/models/users/user_contact.php** the namespace has to be"
" ``namespace App\\Models\\Users;`` and the model path in the version 4 "
"should look like this: **app/Models/Users/UserContact.php**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:34
msgid ""
"The new Model in CI4 has a lot of built-in methods. For example, the "
"``find($id)`` method. With this you can find data where the primary key "
"is equal to ``$id``. Inserting data is also easier than before. In CI4 "
"there is an ``insert($data)`` method. You can optionally make use of all "
"those built-in methods and migrate your code to the new methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/installation/upgrade_models.rst:37
msgid "You can find more information to those methods in :doc:`../models/model`."
msgstr ""

